<title>RUSSIA: WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - to Jan 1.</title>
<headline>WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - to Jan 1.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airports in the southern Russian cities of Rostov-on-Don and Sochi may be closed on December 28, 29 and January 1 due to strong winds and low clouds, the Russian Weather Service said on Friday.</p>
<p>It predicted conditions would allow flights in those areas on December 30 and 31.</p>
<p>Flights in the Russian Far East may be postponed at airports on Sakhalin island and Magadan and Khabarovsk regions on January 1 due to strong winds and snow storms, the service said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
